# fixedbugs, defect 168, lane cb4, 2026-10-02.
#
# Symptom: built in one `build/` with
# `tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-168-a-record-leaving-out-a-member-beside-a-same-named-header`,
# whose header has this one's name and gives `E` a member `y` this record
# leaves out, the second of the two replayed the first's verdict: that
# program built at exit 0, a record leaving `y` out read as complete, or this
# one stopped at exit 2, *no member named 'y' in 'E'*. Cause: the layout
# check's key named the screen's text and not the source's directory, so the
# `-I` that finds each header was outside it. The key now names every word
# the probe compiles under and what the headers resolve to, and this builds
# and prints, after the other or not.

extern "fixedbugs-168-beside.h"
    record E
        x: i32
    function hero_168_make(x: i32) -> E

function main()
    p = hero_168_make(x: 1)
    q = hero_168_make(x: 1)
    print(p == q)
    print(p.x)
